Build type: manifest (extracts Debian bookworm i386 packages, no compile)
Source: https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/m/mesa/
 - libgl1-mesa-dri_22.3.6-1+deb12u2_i386.deb
 - libglx-mesa0_22.3.6-1+deb12u2_i386.deb
 - libegl-mesa0_22.3.6-1+deb12u2_i386.deb
Build order: 32-bit libraries, alongside the other Lib32-* packages; runtime
companion to the 64-bit Mesa recipe (mesa-core/Mesa/25.3.6).
Purpose: 32-bit DRI drivers + GLX/EGL backends so 32-bit games/clients on the
live ISO fall back to software rendering (llvmpipe) when no 32-bit proprietary
driver exists. Extracted from Debian i386 debs rather than compiled: there is
no 32-bit compiler chain in this build and 22.3.6 matches the era of the
other Lib32-* payloads.
Installs to $target/lib32/dri/*.so, libGLX_mesa.so.0*, libGLX_indirect.so.0*,
libEGL_mesa.so.0*.
Version is 22.3.6, matching the Debian bookworm debs it extracts; the recipe
directory name is what Compile matches on, so the deb version must be tracked
here. (It was earlier frozen at 22.3.5 while the debs were already 22.3.6, which
made the directory name disagree with every URL in the recipe.)

Extra debs: only `url` is fetched by Compile.  libglx-mesa0 and libegl-mesa0
have no per-file URL slot, so `pre_install` fetches them itself and verifies
them against `deb_glx_md5` / `deb_egl_md5` (md5, and size recorded above):
 - libglx-mesa0_22.3.6-1+deb12u2_i386.deb  155936  2837a46b052da880ac42de65ac839f25
 - libegl-mesa0_22.3.6-1+deb12u2_i386.deb  123636  4ff1f98ddcb19b62f1ba691752fc7aaf
They are cached in /Data/Compile/Archives under their URL basenames, and reused
if present (`[ -s "$deb" ]`), so a rebuild does not re-download them.
Field order in the pre_install loop is `name|url|md5` with "|" delimiters,
deliberately not ":": the URL contains "https:", and `${rest%%:*}` would cut the
URL down to the bare string "https" -- which is what broke the first forced
build (libglx-mesa0 download handed to curl as the URL `https`).
